{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8DhAvC8Uc4fYmEGjnAY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Exa charges about **$7 per 1,000 standard searches**, or $0.007 per request. That comes from search snippets of Exa's pricing docs, not the full page. Older sources show $5 per 1,000, which looks outdated.\n\n- **What the base price covers:** 10 results per request. Each extra result costs $1 per 1,000 results.\n- **Deep Search:** $12 per 1,000 requests.\n- **Deep-Reasoning Search:** $15 per 1,000 requests.\n- **Page contents:** Billed separately, at $1 per 1,000 pages per content type.\n- **Enterprise:** Custom pricing with volume discounts.\n\nThe Deep Search, Deep-Reasoning and contents prices come from a third-party listing (Respan). Check Exa's pricing page before you budget around them.\n\nSources:\n- [Exa pricing docs](https://exa.ai/docs/reference/pricing)\n- [Exa pricing (markdown)](https://exa.ai/docs/reference/pricing.md)\n- [Exa pricing explained – fastcrw](https://fastcrw.com/blog/exa-pricing-explained)\n- [Exa plans & pricing – CostBench](https://costbench.com/software/web-scraping/exa/)\n- [Exa – Respan](https://www.respan.ai/market-map/exa)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":909,"cache_read_input_tokens":18572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":909},"output_tokens":447,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"619513fd-a347-44a8-9025-6a328c737e2d","uuid":"bf1725d0-cdb2-4cba-924f-f9ec75e475e7","timestamp":"2026-10-17T17:40:32.235Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8DhAgoMpyHifHMq4e4Z"}
